    "statement": {
      "en": "This level is set in Alberta. Discover Canada says Alberta is the country's largest producer of oil and gas, and that its northern oil sands are being developed into a major energy source. It also says the province is renowned for agriculture, and above all for the vast cattle ranches that help make Canada a major beef producer.",
      "fr": "Ce niveau se déroule en Alberta. Discover Canada dit que l'Alberta est le plus grand producteur de pétrole et de gaz du pays, et que ses sables bitumineux du nord deviennent une grande source d'énergie. Le guide dit aussi que la province est réputée pour son agriculture, et surtout pour les vastes ranchs de bovins qui font du Canada un grand producteur de bœuf."
    },
    "fact": {
      "factual": true,
      "source": {
        "sourceId": "discover-canada",
        "chapter": "Canada's Regions",
        "page": 101,
        "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/corporate/publications-manuals/discover-canada.html",
        "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
        "asOf": "2026-09-09T00:00:00Z",
        "volatile": false,
        "quote": "Alberta is the largest producer of oil and gas, and the oil sands in the north are being developed as a major energy source."
      },
      "verification": {
        "status": "verified",
        "model": "claude-opus-5",
        "checkedAt": "2026-09-17T18:50:32Z",
        "sourceHash": "fd51046981916115cc39b989e9eedd3ab2c5943aeb7e0fe4e237e13a0da7c836",
        "evidence": "Alberta is the most populous Prairie province. The province, and the world-famous Lake Louise in the Rocky Mountains, were both named after Princess Louise Caroline Alberta … Alberta is the largest producer of oil and gas, and the oil sands in the north are being developed as a major energy source. Alberta is also renowned for agriculture, especially for the vast cattle ranches that make Canada one of the world’s major beef producers."
      }
    },
